  943:    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  944:    // These are functions that work on all nodes/sides of the element.
  945:    // They use a standard, but not well known, way of accessing the fields of the nodes.
  946:    //
  947:    // An example of how to use these functions is:
  948:    //   
  949:    //    getNodalValues(L, &Node::compZCoord, zLAtNodes);
  950:    // 
  951:    // Where L is the level at which the field is to be interpolated. The field can be either
  952:    // a double (depth), an array (u[nvrt]), or a function that depends on the level (Node::compZCoord(int k)). 
  953:    // There are different versions of getNodalValues for each of these cases.
  954: 
